# BACKEND ENGINEERING STANDARD

Respect the backend framework and conventions already used by the project.

Before modifying backend behavior:
- inspect routes;
- inspect controllers;
- inspect services/use cases;
- inspect models/entities;
- inspect requests/validators;
- inspect policies/authorization;
- inspect migrations;
- inspect tests.

## GENERAL RULES

- Validate input at the appropriate boundary.
- Authorize actions explicitly.
- Keep business rules in an appropriate domain/service layer.
- Avoid fat controllers when the project architecture supports services/use cases.
- Avoid duplicated business logic.
- Use transactions for operations that must be atomic.
- Handle expected failures explicitly.
- Do not expose sensitive internal data.
- Do not log secrets, tokens or credentials.
- Use pagination for potentially large collections.
- Consider N+1 queries.
- Consider indexes for frequently filtered/joined columns.
- Preserve API contracts unless the change explicitly requires a breaking change.

## DATABASE CHANGES

Before changing schema:
- inspect existing migrations;
- inspect model relationships;
- inspect queries;
- inspect API consumers;
- consider existing data;
- consider rollback/deployment order.

Never casually modify an existing migration that may already have been applied. Prefer a new migration when appropriate.
